      "citations": null,
      "text": "This script takes the CMA as the average of the two conservative-investment portfolios (Small LoINV and Big LoINV) minus the average of the two aggressive-investment portfolios (Small HiINV and Big HiINV), using the value-weighted monthly returns. It reads the first (value-weighted monthly) table only, locates columns by header name, and treats -99.99 and -999 as missing.\n\n```python\nimport re\nimport pandas as pd\nimport numpy as np\n\nSRC = \"6_Portfolios_ME_INV_2x3.csv\"\nOUT = \"output.csv\"\n\n\ndef norm(s):\n    return re.sub(r\"\\s+\", \" \", s.strip()).upper()\n\n\ndef main():\n    with open(SRC, encoding=\"latin-1\") as f:\n        lines = f.read().splitlines()\n\n    # Locate the header of the first (value-weighted monthly) table.\n    hdr = None\n    for i, l in enumerate(lines):\n        if l.startswith(\",\") and \"SMALL\" in l.upper() and \"LOINV\" in l.upper():\n            hdr = i\n            break\n    if hdr is None:\n        raise RuntimeError(\"Could not find header line in input file\")\n\n    cols = [norm(c) for c in lines[hdr].split(\",\")][1:]\n\n    def idx(name):\n        target = norm(name)\n        for k, c in enumerate(cols):\n            if c == target:\n                return k\n        raise RuntimeError(f\"Column {name} not found in header: {cols}\")\n\n    i_sl = idx(\"SMALL LoINV\")\n    i_sh = idx(\"SMALL HiINV\")\n    i_bl = idx(\"BIG LoINV\")\n    i_bh = idx(\"BIG HiINV\")\n    ncols = len(cols)\n\n    records = []\n    started = False\n    for l in lines[hdr + 1:]:\n        s = l.strip()\n        if not s:\n            if started:\n                break\n            continue\n        parts = [p.strip() for p in s.split(\",\")]\n        if re.fullmatch(r\"\\d{6}\", parts[0]):\n            started = True\n            vals = []\n            for k in range(ncols):\n                if k + 1 < len(parts):\n                    try:\n                        v = float(parts[k + 1])\n                    except ValueError:\n                        v = np.nan\n                else:\n                    v = np.nan\n                if v in (-99.99, -999.0):\n                    v = np.nan\n                vals.append(v)\n            records.append((int(parts[0]), vals))\n        else:\n            if started:\n                break\n\n    rows = []\n    for date, vals in records:\n        sl, sh, bl, bh = vals[i_sl], vals[i_sh], vals[i_bl], vals[i_bh]\n        cma = 0.5 * (sl + bl) - 0.5 * (sh + bh)\n        if np.isnan(cma):\n            continue\n        rows.append((date, cma))\n\n    out = pd.DataFrame(rows, columns=[\"date\", \"value\"])\n    out[\"date\"] = out[\"date\"].astype(int)\n    out.to_csv(OUT, index=False)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```",
